"},{"sourceUnit":{"$ref":"5436"},"sourceKey":"equal","destinationUnit":{"$ref":"5428"},"destinationKey":"a","guid":"9fc65ac9-9cd9-457a-888a-0dfa9012dcad","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ValueConnection"},{"sourceUnit":{"$ref":"5457"},"sourceKey":"equal","destinationUnit":{"$ref":"5441"},"destinationKey":"a","guid":"c093028b-bf87-4adf-9e1b-1fe02f11941b","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ValueConnection"},{"sourceUnit":{"$ref":"5428"},"sourceKey":"result","destinationUnit":{"$ref":"5461"},"destinationKey":"b","guid":"562e0d27-1f0e-4e4a-971d-4de41c1a5dac","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ValueConnection"},{"sourceUnit":{"$ref":"5441"},"sourceKey":"result","destinationUnit":{"$ref":"5461"},"destinationKey":"a","guid":"aba326e0-3f51-416b-85ef-5662832a6910","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ValueConnection"},{"position":{"xMin":-1814.0,"yMin":394.0,"xMax":-1100.0,"yMax":700.0},"title":"Correct
      way to check if my AI has card in hand AND add them to possibleCards list","body":"\n1)
      Go trough my Cards In Hand (Game Objects) with For Each loop\n\n2) Get the
      Card Display component (from my Game Objects, I make a reference to the Card
      Display component which contains my Scriptable Objects)\n\n3) Get the Card
      Data component (the Card Data component is what it makes me possible to make
      a reference to my Scripting Objects from my GameObjects)\n\n4) Get Card Name
      (refers to my Scriptable Objects)\n-> This one is tricky : My Card Data component
      contains which specific Card is attached to it\nSo I can get my cards data
      (value, name, color, ...) from my Card Display component \n\n5) Connect my
